    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.minimum_weight_matching - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.minimum_weight_matching.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.minimum_weight_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find a minimum-weight matching among the matchings with the most edges.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.minimum_weight_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find a minimum-weight matching among the matchings with the most edges.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.minimum_weight_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Find a minimum-weight matching among the matchings with the most edges.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind a minimum-weight matching among the matchings with the most edges.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L77750-L77853){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.minimum_weight_matching(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Minimum weight matching](../assets/graphs/minimum-weight-matching.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Four drivers A, B, C, D with the extra driving time of each possible pair as edge weights: A–B (2), C–D (3), A–C (1), B–D (6), and A–D (4). Among the matchings that pair everyone, the cheapest is A–B and C–D, in the accent color, total 2 + 3 = 5; the other edges are faded. The card notes that taking the cheapest edge A–C (1) would force B–D (6), a total of 7.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA matching is a set of edges with no shared endpoints. This method first makes the\nmatching as large as possible (as many pairs as the graph allows) and, among all such\nmatchings, returns one with the smallest total weight. On a graph with a perfect\nmatching, that is the cheapest way to pair up every node. It is the right tool when\nedges are costs (distances, prices, travel times) and everyone should be paired.\n\nRequiring a maximum number of edges matters: without it, the cheapest matching would\nsimply be empty. Edge direction is ignored, self-loops are never chosen, and among\nparallel edges only the lightest can be chosen.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph's `weighted`\n    flag. Without weights every maximum matching is equally cheap.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The IDs of the matched edges, in ascending order.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If an edge weight is not finite.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nAs in NetworkX, every weight $w$ is replaced by $W + 1 - w$, where $W$ is the largest\nweight, and a maximum-weight matching of maximum cardinality is computed with Edmonds'\nblossom algorithm (see `maximum_weight_matching()`). Since all matchings considered have the\nsame number of edges $k$, maximizing $\\sum (W + 1 - w) = k(W + 1) - \\sum w$ minimizes\nthe original total. It runs in $O(V^3)$ time.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~maximum_weight_matching`) \n\n:   The heaviest matching.\n\n[](`~bipartite_minimum_weight_full_matching`) \n\n:   The same for the two sides of a bipartite graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nFour delivery drivers are paired into two-person teams, and each edge is the extra\ndriving time if the two share a route. The cheapest single edge, `A`-`C`, isn't used:\npairing `A` with `C` would force `B` and `D` together, for 7 in all instead of 5:\n\n::: {#47566517 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ng = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\", 2.0), (\"C\", \"D\", 3.0), (\"A\", \"C\", 1.0),\n     (\"B\", \"D\", 6.0), (\"A\", \"D\", 4.0)]\n)\nteams = g.minimum_weight_matching()\n\nlabel = g.get_label_from_id\n[[label(n) for n in g.get_node_ids_by_edge_id(e)] for e in teams]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['A', 'B'], ['C', 'D']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Covering seven tasks in the fewest hours\n\n`teams()` links the 8 workers of a made-up software team to the 8 tasks of a release that\neach can do, weighted by the hours it would take them. At most seven of the tasks can be\ncovered. Of the ways to cover seven, the quickest takes 32 hours and leaves DevOps to\nwait:\n\n::: {#a8c1ba2c .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam = ec.teams()\nmatched = team.minimum_weight_matching()\n\nlabel = team.get_label_from_id\nends = team.get_node_ids_by_edge_id\ndone = {label(n) for e in matched for n in ends(e)}\ntasks = team.get_node_df().filter(side=\"task\")[\"label\"]\n\n(\n    len(matched),\n    sum(team.get_edge(e).weight for e in matched),\n    [t for t in tasks if t not in done],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(7, 32.0, ['DevOps'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#792ae854 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam.layout_bipartite(align=\"horizontal\", aspect_ratio=0.4).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight_edges=matched, label_by=\"label\", height=300\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4